WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.670
CARTER MORGAN: This week,
we're talking about AI from A

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.230
to Z. I'm Carter Morgan.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.730
And welcome to "This
Week in Cloud,"

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.800
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.710
We created AI Hub
to make it easier

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.910
to collaborate in the cloud.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.800
And it's constantly evolving.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.110
More comprehensive labeling
for assets and the ability

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.810
to favorite assets you use
regularly are just a few

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:19.950
of the ways.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.260
You might notice a few
changes to the home page too.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.780
Get the full brief
on the cloud blog.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.350
If you're already using AI
Platform Prediction to run

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:29.340
ML models, you can
now take advantage

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.700
of continuous evaluation to
keep those models in top form.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.560
We'll assign real
human reviewers

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.543
to compare samples from your
models to ground truth tables,

00:00:37.543 --> 00:00:39.960
giving you a clear picture of
how your model is performing

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.410
across time.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:42.510
It's all on the tutorial.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.110
Check it out.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.350
Speaking of better
ML models, are you

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.080
looking to analyze your
conversational experience

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.780
to improve customer
satisfaction and get insights

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.820
into top customer queries?

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.680
Priyanka Vergadia
has a great post

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.110
outlining how you can send
data from your conversational

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:01.050
experience built on Dialogflow
directly into BigQuery

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.550
for further analysis.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.530
Go peep that.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.450
Cloud Storage
Platform already makes

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:07.860
it easy to store your data.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.630
But knowing how to
optimize your storage

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.270
spend for your specific
needs, that calls

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:13.470
for a little more guidance.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.870
And we've got a great
resource to get you started.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:19.110
Learn best practices, like
setting up a lifecycle policy.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.557
Then grab your broom and
dustpan and get to work.

00:01:21.557 --> 00:01:23.640
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.930
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:27.298
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:27.298 --> 00:01:28.590
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.000
And in the meantime, we'll
see you in the cloud.

